tal": 6.88, "baseline_margin": 12.34, "analyst_adjustment": 0.16, "key_factors": ["Colorado's D+6 partisan lean and recent Democratic dominance in statewide races", "Expert ratings unanimous for Democrats, four of six at Solid or Safe D", "Prediction markets on three platforms converge near 97% for a Democratic win", "No public general-election polls; open seat with roughly even fundraising limits precision"], "rationale": "Colorado's partisan lean, a unanimous expert-rater consensus, and market pricing near 97% all point to Phil Weiser holding the open seat, and fundraising is roughly even with Marx burning cash quickly, so nothing justifies moving off a double-digit Democratic margin.", "watch": "The first public general-election polls or a standout debate performance by Victor Marx could narrow the expected margin.", "confidence": "medium", "notes": ["No usable general-election polls; forecast rests on fundamentals and expert ratings.", "Open seat: Jared Polis (D) is not on the ballot."]}, "overview": "Colorado's governorship is open this year as Jared Polis is term-limited, and Attorney General Phil Weiser carries the Democratic banner against Republican Victor Marx. The state has leaned about six points Democratic recently, and every major race rating published in late September places the contest in the Democratic column, four of them in the strongest category. Betting markets on three platforms converge near 97% for a Democratic win.\n\nNo public general-election polls are available, so the outlook rests on the state's partisan lean, the ratings consensus, and market pricing. Fundraising has been roughly even, though Marx is spending at a rapid pace, and the first debate between the two major nominees was called off. Independent and minor-party candidates, including Greg Lopez, are on the ballot but are not viewed as competitive.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.9695, "margin": 12.28}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.9628, "margin": 12.0}, {"